# FramePilot — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env.local` only if you are working on the optional v2 cloud layer.
# `.env.local` is git-ignored and must never be committed.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1 (the currently deployed experience) needs NO environment variables.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FramePilot v1 is local-first: direction is generated by a deterministic local
# engine and everything you save is kept in your browser's localStorage. There
# are no API routes, no model calls, and no database on this path.
# `npm install && npm run dev` is enough, and Vercel needs no variables set for
# a successful build. Leaving every value below empty keeps v1 fully working.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v2 (optional, in progress) — Supabase foundation
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both variables below are browser-safe by design. The publishable key is meant
# to be shipped to the client; Row Level Security in the database is what
# actually protects user data, not the secrecy of this key.
#
# Leave these empty and `isSupabaseConfigured()` reports false, so any future
# v2 surface renders an "unavailable" state instead of breaking v1.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Earlier alias for the key above — NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY is also
# accepted by lib/supabase/env.ts, but NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is preferred.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT in this file
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# - SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — bypasses RLS. Never place it in this repo, never
#   prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_, and never read it from client code. It belongs
#   only in a trusted server environment, introduced in a later phase.
# - GEMINI_API_KEY / model credentials — server-only, and no model integration
#   exists yet. See docs/v2-architecture.md for the planned trust boundary.
